{"findings":[{"check_id":"CKV_AWS_88","title":"Public IP address attached to EC2 instance","resource":"aws_eip.ip","severity":"MEDIUM","explanation":"The Elastic IP is directly associated with the EC2 instance, giving it a persistent public IP address. This increases the instance's external attack surface even though its security group rules are not shown in this file."}],"patched_code":"resource "aws_eip" "ip" {
  domain = "vpc"
}
","fix_summary":"Removed the Elastic IP association from the EC2 instance so the instance is not assigned a persistent public IP by this resource. The Elastic IP resource is retained and explicitly scoped to the VPC domain."}
